  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixed:\n- Identifier quoting now escapes embedded double quotes, so a table, schema, or\n  column name that contains '\"' is quoted correctly in the generated COPY\n  command (for example, My\"Table becomes \"My\"\"Table\"). The previous\n  already-quoted heuristic, which skipped quoting when the name started or ended\n  with a quote, has been removed.\n- The README usage example now calls WriteDataAsync, the actual API, instead of\n  the nonexistent InsertAsync, and spells the dependency \"Npgsql\".\n\nChanged:\n- CreateBulkContext now validates its arguments: it throws ArgumentNullException\n  for a null connection and ArgumentException for a null or whitespace table or\n  schema name. WriteDataAsync throws ArgumentNullException when the entity\n  collection is null, and the Map* methods throw ArgumentException for a null or\n  whitespace column name.\n- Mapping the same column twice now throws InvalidOperationException naming the\n  duplicated column, instead of silently producing an invalid COPY command that\n  failed later on the server.",
